  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Classification
    
    Hush☽ Twilight is a Nightshelf suppression practice formally classified as a weaponized derivative of ☽Silv-glaciere☽ Arts — specifically the reshaping operation, narrowed to negate perception at the point of formation rather than rewriting memory afterward. Nightshelf theorists designate it an **anti-source practice**: it draws on captured fire and pressure-depth to cancel aurora-light through controlled opposition. A depth-sourced art aimed against the surface.
    
    Suppression techniques of this general type predate the unified ☽Silv-glaciere☽ school by an indeterminate period. The *Nighted~ Lantern*, a Nightshelf grimoire of contested reliability, describes comparable practices in its third chapter. Whether Hush☽ Twilight is a refinement of those older workings or an independent derivation discovered under duress remains unresolved.
    
    ## Discovery and Origins
    
    The canonical account holds that Hush☽ Twilight was first identified during the Orca Incursion, radiating from Veil☽ Sasvaeumis~ — a volcanic glass and shadow-steel weapon crafted by Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane, a Nightshelf artificer — in the depths near ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~, a subterranean Nightshelf site. Whether Augur ☽'Milucaum~ created the effect or merely gave it a vessel is a distinction the sources decline to make.
    
    ## Mechanism and Cost
    
    The technique does not extinguish light or eliminate sound. It presses them down — aurora-glow dims as though submerged, sound thickens into a weight that will not carry past the caster's own beak. Witnesses to violence conducted under its influence see movement but hear nothing, and later struggle to recall that anything occurred. The effect is not amnesia in the ☽Silv-glaciere☽ sense; it is closer to the ice ceasing to record.
    
    The cost is personal and cumulative. Each casting requires the practitioner to surrender one small detail of something loved — a melody, a face, a name. Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~, founder of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ and the first documented master of the practice, exhibited physical trembling after each working. ☽'Otrolal the Watchful — whose name, I note elsewhere in this edition, follows orca rather than penguin phonemic patterns — employs it in the tunnels beneath ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ to guard breach-points where deep-corruption surfaces. Some practitioners cease. Others continue until they have emptied themselves into serviceable silence.
    
    ## Propagation Beyond the Nightshelf
    
    Nightshelf analysts have raised — and the record has confirmed — that Hush☽ Twilight, once taught to an outsider, functions as a self-propagating practice independent of Nightshelf ice or institutional knowledge. Plunge-Caller Oeichowei, leader of the Aurora Stack splinter faction known as The Pinnacle, successfully deployed the technique near the Radiant Aurora-harp, a surface site with no Nightshelf ice substrate. The implications for taxonomic control are severe and, to my knowledge, unaddressed by any governing body.
    
    ## Material Embedding
    
    The practice embeds in objects as well as spaces. The *Nighted~ Lantern*'s own fracture-mark, inflicted by the ice-scream Mbra∴silentiu, contains a localized Hush☽ Twilight effect — its pages at that point no longer hold memory. When channeled through shadow-steel weapons such as Veil☽ Sasvaeumis~, the suppression enters each wound directly: cuts do not bleed but exhale, silence radiating from the edge inward.
    
    Hush☽ Twilight manifests at multiple Nightshelf sites, including ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~, Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius, and the Glow-Fissure. It has been corrupted at ☽'thaw Iasnolica~, though the nature of that corruption remains inadequately documented.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771587189474_0", anchor: "it is closer to the ice ceasing to record", text: "I chose this phrasing over several alternatives and I am no longer certain it was the right one. The Foundation Depths preserve ice-memory from every era — violence, tenderness, catastrophe, boredom. The ice records indiscriminately. It does not choose. For a practice to suppress that function implies either that Hush☽ Twilight operates on a source-level the ice cannot overrule, or that the ice *can* choose and simply never had reason to before. Either possibility reorganizes what I thought I understood about my own archive.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587189474_1", anchor: "comparable practices in its third chapter", text: "Third chapter. Cross-reference my annotation on Jark Rankzule, the orca who claims inability to read past chapter three of that same grimoire. One wonders what specifically arrests progress at that threshold.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771587189474_2", anchor: "surrender one small detail of something loved", text: "The Crypt-Chancellor pours a second cup that cools untouched. Every time. I wrote about this in her entry — the refusal to update the count. Now place that habit beside this cost mechanism and ask: is she still counting, or has she forgotten what the second cup was for and pours it anyway? The trembling suggests she knows. The persistence suggests it no longer matters whether she does.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587189474_3", anchor: "self-propagating practice independent of Nightshelf ice or institutional knowledge", text: "How extraordinary that they taught it to anyone at all. A silence-art whose entire tactical value depends on secrecy, released to an Aurora splinter faction led by a penguin the Nightshelf cannot control. Mandatum∴absconditu — survival demands secrecy — and yet here we are.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
